// v16.xx, HIS ORDER 2026-10-12 (about 21:48): "improve dsound generally, look for other actions that don't have disntinct noises
// yetr and add them". THE NEW VOICES. A table of short recipes, each a few layers of filtered noise (the crack and the body of a
// hit) and pitched tones (the thump, the ping, the whine), played through the same mix bus, pan and wall lowpass as every placed
// sound (blip hands them over after it has placed the sound). One small player makes them all, so a new noise is a line of numbers
// and a few nodes for a fraction of a second. Each voice keeps its own minimum gap, so twenty of them in one fight never stack into
// mush. The noise inside a recipe is made once per audio device and kept, from Math.random only, never a seeded draw; nothing here
// touches game state and nothing plays under G.sim (blip returns first). Layer fields: n (noise seconds), pw (its decay), ft, fq, q
// (its filter); or ty, f0, f1, d (a tone sweeping f0 to f1 over d), atk and rel (its swell and tail), fq and fq1 (an optional filter
// that sweeps); g (level), at (delay), rep, ev and mul (repeat it rep times ev apart, the pitch times mul each time).
// MACHINE GUNS: every machine fired the pillager rifle sound (fireWeapon passed no gun id for a machine, so the shot fell back to
// the rifle), so a sentry across the street sounded exactly like a man with a rifle, or your own. Now each machine fires its own:
// the sentry a fast electric snap with a servo tick, the warden a deep cannon thump with a metal slap, the Overseer the same an
// octave down and louder, the bulwark a dull plated bark, the pillbox a hollow turret pop. The pillbox also played the rifle crack
// a second time on top of its shot (its own sfx after fireWeapon), so each pillbox round was two rifle cracks; that one is gone.
